## Cap data-assets imports (default 40)

Context: Importing an entire Unity Catalog schema can load far more tables than
ontology generation can handle. Settings → Global now exposes an import cap
(default 40, range 1–500) enforced in the picker UI and on the metadata load
backend.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/uc/MetadataService.py
   Clamp import limit; cap schema-wide and selected-table loads.
2. src/back/objects/session/GlobalConfigService.py
   Persist data_assets_import_limit (default 40).
3. src/back/objects/domain/WorkspaceUiSettings.py
   GET/save helpers for the Global setting.
4. src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   Delegators for the new setting.
5. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
   GET /settings/data-assets-import-limit and POST save.
6. src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py
   Pass the cap into load paths; list-tables returns import_limit.
7. src/back/objects/domain/_metadata_tasks.py
   Async metadata load honours import_limit.
8. src/front/templates/settings.html
   Global number input, default 40.
9. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   Load and save the import limit with other Global settings.
10. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-metadata.js
    Selection respects remaining slots; banner shows the cap.
11. tests/units/core/test_metadata_mgt.py
    Clamp, cap, and limit-reached coverage.
12. tests/units/front/test_data_assets_import_limit.py
    Settings HTML/JS and Domain picker contracts.
13. tests/units/domain/test_list_schema_tables_object_kind.py
    list-tables payload includes import_limit 40.
14. docs/user-guide.md
    Document the default 40-asset import cap.
15. docs/api.md
    Document the GET/POST settings endpoints.

